<header><p class="st-kicker">princely state · Indian princely states</p><h1 class="st-title">Dhar State</h1><p class="st-meta">1728 CE – 1948 CE (approx.) · capital Dhar</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Maratha Puar state in Malwa centred on Dhar, the old Paramara capital of King Bhoja.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Udaji Rao and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anand-rao-puar">Anand Rao Puar</a> were <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Maratha</a> commanders active in the conquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malwa">Malwa</a>. Around 1728–32 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peshwa">Peshwa</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baji-rao-i">Baji Rao I</a> confirmed Anand Rao in Dhar, a city with a long royal past as the 11th-century capital of the Paramara king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bhoja-paramara">Bhoja</a>. The Puars of Dhar were related to the Puars of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/dewas-senior">Dewas Senior</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/dewas-junior">Dewas Junior</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Dhar was badly weakened by the wars of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scindias">Scindia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holkars">Holkar</a> around 1800 and recovered under British protection after the treaty of 1819. Its ruler was briefly deprived of the state after the revolt of 1857, which was restored in 1860 minus the Bairasia district. A <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharaja">Maharaja</a> governed a mainly <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinduism">Hindu</a> population; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bhojshala">Bhoj Shala</a> and the Dhar fort are its main monuments.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After accession to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, Dhar merged into <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/madhya-bharat">Madhya Bharat</a> in 1948 and became part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madhya-pradesh">Madhya Pradesh</a> in 1956.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/dhar-state.jpg" alt="Dhar State" width="200" height="134"><figcaption>Image: The original uploader was Nataraja at French Wikipedia. · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Drapeau_Dhar.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1728 CE – 1948 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>princely state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Dhar</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Anand Rao Puar</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Malvi, Marathi</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Dhar</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1838&amp;focus=dhar-state" aria-label="Dhar State on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6695 1343 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Dhar State lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7015 1599L6991 1757M7015 1599L7364 1601M7015 1599L7364 1602M7015 1599L7064 1471"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6991 1757h0M7364 1601h0M7364 1602h0M7064 1471h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7015 1599h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7015 1599h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Dhar. <a href="/atlas?year=1838&amp;focus=dhar-state">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
